  }
}"}

{"reason": "The execution log confirms overfitting (train loss 0.31 vs val loss 0.69) and an inefficient learning rate schedule (first 5 epochs barely learn, LR at 5e-6). The initial plan already targets both. Historical experiments show that successful improvements came from adopting CyclicLR with realistic initial LR (e.g., 1e-2) and stronger regularization (dropout+LayerNorm). One similar experiment achieved validation logloss <0.4 with these changes. Therefore the modules 'training_evaluation' and 'model_design' are selected to apply the refined changes: a more aggressive OneCycleLR scheduler and increased dropout with LayerNorm.", "module": ["training_evaluation", "model_design"], "plan": {"training_evaluation": "Replace the warmup + cosine annealing scheduler with a OneCycleLR scheduler (max_lr=1e-2, pct_start=0.3, div_factor=20, final_div_factor=1e4) and reduce total epochs to 20. This is based on historical success with immediate high initial LR eliminating wasted warmup epochs and achieving best validation by epoch 12-14. Implementation: use torch.optim.lr_scheduler.OneCycleLR with the same optimizer; increase gradient clipping max_norm to 5.0 to prevent divergence with higher LR. Interface: train_and_evaluate function signature unchanged.", "model_design": "Increase all dropout probabilities from 0.3 to 0.4 and replace BatchNorm1d with LayerNorm in the tfidf_branch and stylo_branch. This directly addresses the overfitting gap (train loss 0.31 vs val 0.69) as historical experiments showed similar adjustments narrowing the gap by ~0.15. LayerNorm is more robust for heterogeneous features and stabilizes training with high LR. Implementation: modify Sequential blocks in MultiInputClassifier, keeping all layer dimensions and the CrossAttentionFusion module identical. Interface: MultiInputClassifier class signature and forward unchanged."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The execution log confirms overfitting (train loss 0.31 vs val loss 0.69) and an inefficient learning rate schedule (first 5 epochs barely learn, LR at 5e-6). The initial plan already targets both. Historical experiments show that successful improvements came from adopting CyclicLR with realistic initial LR (e.g., 1e-2) and stronger regularization (dropout+LayerNorm). One similar experiment achieved validation logloss <0.4 with these changes. Therefore the modules 'training_evaluation' and 'model_design' are selected to apply the refined changes: a more aggressive OneCycleLR scheduler and increased dropout with LayerNorm.",
  "module": ["training_evaluation", "model_design"],
  "plan": {
