ects TF-IDF and stylo features to same dimension, applies multi-head attention (4 heads, 256 dim) with stylo as query and TF-IDF as key/value, then combines via gated residual. The fused output is fed to the classifier. This is directly informed by a successful historical experiment. Implementation: create CrossAttentionFusion class and modify MultiInputClassifier.forward accordingly. Interface constraints: MultiInputClassifier class signature and forward(tfidf, stylo) remain unchanged.", "training_evaluation": "Add a linear learning rate warmup for 5 epochs before cosine annealing, and implement differential learning rates: set lr=1e-4 for tfidf_branch and stylo_branch parameters (slower to preserve learned features), and lr=1e-3 for all other parameters (faster adaptation). Increase total epochs to 35 with patience increased to 10. This stabilizes the new attention mechanism and follows the successful historical pattern. Implementation: modify scheduler to use LambdaLR with linear warmup, adjust optimizer parameter groups accordingly. Interface constraints: train_and_evaluate function signature unchanged."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
